<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11109" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀοίδ-ιμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sung of, famous in
			song</i> or <i>story,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.79
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				135
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				8.59
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προφάταν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					6.6
				</span></i>
			; from <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				76
			</span></i>) downwds. a favourite epith. of Athens; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πόμα</span> a <i>glorious</i> draught,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>N.</u>
				3.79
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. εὐνομίῃσιν</span>
			<i>famous</i> for his justice, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				7.94
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Nisaea</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tim.</u>
				38
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				2.82
			</span></i>, etc.: 
				Sup.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				34
			</span></i>:—only once in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, and in bad sense, <i>notorious, infamous,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς . . ἀνθρώποισι πελώμεθ᾽ ἀοίδιμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.358
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>won by song,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγρα,</span> of the Sphinx's victims,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				471
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
